WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:05.693
Tonight, the Kremlin is accusing the U.S.

00:00:05.693 --> 00:00:07.800
of an economic war on Russia,

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:10.390
one day after President
Biden's ban on Russian oil

00:00:10.390 --> 00:00:11.590
and other energy imports.

00:00:11.590 --> 00:00:16.260
This is unprecedented,
that a large economy,

00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:20.643
150 million people, has
been literally, walled off

00:00:20.643 --> 00:00:22.350
from the rest of the global economy

00:00:22.350 --> 00:00:24.440
within a matter of days.

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:25.820
Working in unison,

00:00:25.820 --> 00:00:27.730
Western governments have turned Russia

00:00:27.730 --> 00:00:30.450
into the most sanctioned
nation in the world

00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:32.213
and sent their economy tumbling.

00:00:39.243 --> 00:00:40.880
It's a complete 180.

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:45.880
This is the end of an era,
of 30 years of integration.

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:48.473
The hope is,

00:00:48.473 --> 00:00:50.810
that by crumbling Russia's economy,

00:00:50.810 --> 00:00:54.563
it will persuade Vladimir Putin
to end his war in Ukraine.

00:00:57.030 --> 00:00:58.400
The only thing that we can do

00:00:58.400 --> 00:01:00.610
with these sanctions is to bleed him dry

00:01:00.610 --> 00:01:02.020
so that there is no left

00:01:02.020 --> 00:01:03.420
for him to execute this war.

00:01:05.290 --> 00:01:08.060
The estimates are that the GDP

00:01:08.060 --> 00:01:11.480
of Russia is gonna contract
by 30% immediately.

00:01:11.480 --> 00:01:13.870
30% GDP contraction is the equivalent

00:01:13.870 --> 00:01:16.450
of the Great Depression
that took place in America.

00:01:16.450 --> 00:01:19.176
It's gonna be a savage, horrific effect

00:01:19.176 --> 00:01:22.980
on the Russian people,
on the Russian economy,

00:01:22.980 --> 00:01:25.140
and on everything to do with Russia.

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:26.390
There's not gonna be a single person

00:01:26.390 --> 00:01:28.493
who's unaffected by what's coming.

00:01:38.510 --> 00:01:40.370
In some respects, there's almost a shock

00:01:40.370 --> 00:01:41.603
and awe treatment, with respect

00:01:41.603 --> 00:01:42.960
to some of these sanctions.

00:01:42.960 --> 00:01:45.010
You know, the stock market
has been sort of seized up

00:01:45.010 --> 00:01:47.120
essentially since the
day after the invasion.

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:48.840
You've seen hundreds of companies,

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:50.280
international companies leave.

00:01:50.280 --> 00:01:52.088
So all of that I think has
had an immediate effect

00:01:52.088 --> 00:01:55.673
on the economic fortunes of Russians.

00:01:57.860 --> 00:02:01.550
Will it achieve the
ends that are intended,

00:02:01.550 --> 00:02:04.630
which is to get Putin to stop waging war?

00:02:04.630 --> 00:02:05.980
I'm not so sure about that.

00:02:22.930 --> 00:02:24.903
Putin is the aggressor.

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:27.752
Putin chose this war

00:02:27.752 --> 00:02:29.100
and now he

00:02:29.100 --> 00:02:31.250
and his country will
bear the consequences.

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:34.220
The EU, U.K., USA,

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:37.570
and NATO partners are
pouring military equipment

00:02:37.570 --> 00:02:39.880
and aid into Ukraine,

00:02:39.880 --> 00:02:42.740
but there's a limit to
what they can offer.

00:02:42.740 --> 00:02:44.080
Because the West has decided

00:02:44.080 --> 00:02:47.008
it doesn't wanna engage
militarily with Russia,

00:02:47.008 --> 00:02:47.940
another nuclear power,

00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:49.870
the only tool they've got left

00:02:49.870 --> 00:02:51.996
in the toolbox is sanctions,

00:02:51.996 --> 00:02:55.230
and they're gonna hit them

00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:57.250
with sanctions as hard as they can.

00:02:57.250 --> 00:02:59.590
The Russian oligarch
crack-down continuing.

00:02:59.590 --> 00:03:01.630
Russia's oligarchs, the elite owners,

00:03:01.630 --> 00:03:05.710
and managers of industry,
have been targeted, their jets

00:03:05.710 --> 00:03:09.100
and boats impounded, their
bank accounts frozen.

00:03:09.100 --> 00:03:09.933
We're seeing evidence

00:03:09.933 --> 00:03:12.190
that really, any Russian links are proven

00:03:12.190 --> 00:03:15.810
pretty problematic, whether
that's in business or culture.

00:03:15.810 --> 00:03:17.415
So I've been campaigning for 10 years

00:03:17.415 --> 00:03:19.037
to toughen up on Putin

00:03:19.037 --> 00:03:22.170
and to toughen up on Russian
criminality in London,

00:03:22.170 --> 00:03:24.860
and I felt like I was
knocking on a closed door.

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:26.730
And then all of a sudden, in two weeks,

00:03:26.730 --> 00:03:27.760
everything that I've been trying to do

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:29.803
for 10 years has become possible.

00:03:31.150 --> 00:03:32.130
Bill Browder was

00:03:32.130 --> 00:03:35.960
once the largest foreign
portfolio investor in Russia,

00:03:35.960 --> 00:03:37.220
but after blowing the whistle

00:03:37.220 --> 00:03:40.370
on massive corruption, he was targeted.

00:03:40.370 --> 00:03:41.203
His lawyer

00:03:41.203 --> 00:03:44.070
and friend Sergei Magnitsky was detained,

00:03:44.070 --> 00:03:46.220
allegedly beaten by guards,

00:03:46.220 --> 00:03:47.730
and refused medical care,

00:03:47.730 --> 00:03:50.623
before dying in prison in 2009.

00:03:51.800 --> 00:03:55.500
Well, London is to Russia
as Hong Kong is to China.

00:03:55.500 --> 00:03:59.220
Every Russian who stole
money, every oligarch,

00:03:59.220 --> 00:04:02.620
every corrupt official,
wants a place, a safe place

00:04:02.620 --> 00:04:04.130
to keep that money

00:04:04.130 --> 00:04:07.762
and London has rule of
law, it has property rights

00:04:07.762 --> 00:04:10.100
and most importantly, nobody's gonna ask

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:12.940
any tough questions from
law enforcement here.

00:04:12.940 --> 00:04:15.240
For decades, Russian money was welcomed

00:04:15.240 --> 00:04:16.690
by lawyers, accountants,

00:04:16.690 --> 00:04:19.260
and politicians, even in the face

00:04:19.260 --> 00:04:21.050
of an alleged assassination,

00:04:21.050 --> 00:04:23.933
and attempted assassination on U.K. soil.

00:04:24.931 --> 00:04:26.970
Alexander Litvinenko's death

00:04:26.970 --> 00:04:29.530
from acute radiation sickness was slow

00:04:29.530 --> 00:04:31.578
and agonizing.

00:04:31.578 --> 00:04:32.690
In 2006,

00:04:32.690 --> 00:04:35.460
former KGB officer Alexander Litvinenko,

00:04:35.460 --> 00:04:38.622
a fierce Putin critic,
died after being poisoned.

00:04:38.622 --> 00:04:40.225
Then in 2018,

00:04:40.225 --> 00:04:43.840
former military intelligence
officer Sergei Skripal

00:04:43.840 --> 00:04:45.620
and his daughter, were poisoned

00:04:45.620 --> 00:04:47.710
with the nerve agent Novichok,

00:04:47.710 --> 00:04:50.020
in the English city of Salisbury.

00:04:50.020 --> 00:04:52.810
They lived, but a British
woman who was exposed

00:04:52.810 --> 00:04:55.150
to the nerve agent died.

00:04:55.150 --> 00:04:58.225
So the U.K., historically, took no action

00:04:58.225 --> 00:05:00.280
against anybody for anything.

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:04.170
You could kill people
using nuclear materials

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:05.610
and there would be no consequences.

00:05:05.610 --> 00:05:07.410
You could shut down a whole city

00:05:07.410 --> 00:05:09.210
with banned chemical weapons

00:05:09.210 --> 00:05:10.773
and there'd be no consequences.

00:05:11.690 --> 00:05:14.210
And so, the U.K. has got
a terrible reputation

00:05:14.210 --> 00:05:17.330
as far as permissive attitude

00:05:17.330 --> 00:05:19.033
towards Russian malfeasance.

00:05:20.950 --> 00:05:22.150
The West's response

00:05:22.150 --> 00:05:25.130
to Russia's invasion to
Ukraine has been much stronger

00:05:25.130 --> 00:05:27.190
than anything seen before.

00:05:27.190 --> 00:05:30.340
The U.K., which was criticized
for being slower than the EU

00:05:30.340 --> 00:05:33.433
and USA on sanctions is now in line.

00:05:34.640 --> 00:05:36.730
And I would argue that
the British government

00:05:36.730 --> 00:05:41.330
is now acting appropriately toughly.

00:05:41.330 --> 00:05:42.690
And I'm the biggest critic

00:05:42.690 --> 00:05:44.170
of the British government
when it comes to this

00:05:44.170 --> 00:05:45.470
and I can say that, you know,

00:05:45.470 --> 00:05:47.020
I'm impressed with the sanctions

00:05:47.020 --> 00:05:48.383
that are now being imposed.

00:05:50.130 --> 00:05:50.963
The invasion

00:05:50.963 --> 00:05:53.540
of Ukraine has caused
outrage across Europe,

00:05:53.540 --> 00:05:54.990
and nations that once tried

00:05:54.990 --> 00:05:57.420
to economically integrate with Russia,

00:05:57.420 --> 00:06:00.310
are taking action against
President Vladimir Putin

00:06:00.310 --> 00:06:01.293
and his government.

00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:06.360
I think he completely
underestimated the appetite

00:06:06.360 --> 00:06:10.110
of Western governments to
impose punishing sanctions.

00:06:10.110 --> 00:06:13.110
I think he thought,
not only, would the war

00:06:13.110 --> 00:06:17.200
in Ukraine be as easy as annexing Crimea,

00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:19.000
that it would be over very quickly,

00:06:19.000 --> 00:06:24.000
but he did not count on unity
amongst European countries,

00:06:25.940 --> 00:06:27.150
as well as the U.S.,

00:06:27.150 --> 00:06:30.130
and the U.K., to impose
punishing sanctions

00:06:30.130 --> 00:06:32.713
that would cost their
economies as well as his.

00:06:35.110 --> 00:06:37.939
They're looking at this
incredible coalition,

00:06:37.939 --> 00:06:41.254
you know, Pacific-Atlantic,
you've see the Japanese,

00:06:41.254 --> 00:06:43.230
the Australians, even
jurisdictions like Switzerland

00:06:43.230 --> 00:06:45.070
that have historically stayed far away

00:06:45.070 --> 00:06:47.400
from this kind of thing,
are stepping into the game

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:48.530
and away from the sidelines

00:06:48.530 --> 00:06:50.460
which is just an amazing scene.

00:06:50.460 --> 00:06:51.500
So all of that suggests

00:06:51.500 --> 00:06:53.644
that we are in an unprecedented time.

00:06:53.644 --> 00:06:55.470
And so, unprecedented time means

00:06:55.470 --> 00:06:58.560
that there's gonna be incredible
unprecedented effects,

00:06:58.560 --> 00:06:59.630
frankly both planned

00:06:59.630 --> 00:07:00.830
and unplanned, so I think that we need

00:07:00.830 --> 00:07:02.817
to look for both of those
on the economic side

00:07:02.817 --> 00:07:05.160
and the political side as well.

00:07:05.160 --> 00:07:07.293
The speed and unity of action

00:07:07.293 --> 00:07:11.090
by Western governments has
caught some by surprise.

00:07:11.090 --> 00:07:12.620
After years of disagreement

00:07:12.620 --> 00:07:15.220
between European nations about how

00:07:15.220 --> 00:07:18.350
and if to engage with Putin's Russia,

00:07:18.350 --> 00:07:21.790
EU countries have been
shocked into coalition.

00:07:21.790 --> 00:07:24.009
The Western world has finally
woken up to the threat

00:07:24.009 --> 00:07:28.779
that Russian President
Vladimir Putin poses

00:07:28.779 --> 00:07:32.830
and so the sanctions
have been unprecedented

00:07:32.830 --> 00:07:35.930
in terms of hitting
hard the Russian economy

00:07:35.930 --> 00:07:37.600
from every angle.

00:07:37.600 --> 00:07:41.070
Everything from freezing some

00:07:41.070 --> 00:07:43.860
of the Russian central banks' reserves,

00:07:43.860 --> 00:07:45.100
foreign currency reserves,

00:07:45.100 --> 00:07:48.450
to kicking Russian banks out of SWIFT,

00:07:48.450 --> 00:07:50.313
the financial messaging system,

00:07:51.550 --> 00:07:54.742
limits or bans on Russian oil and gas,

00:07:54.742 --> 00:07:56.623
the list goes on and on.

00:07:56.623 --> 00:08:01.112
And the goal really is to
deal a devastating blow

00:08:01.112 --> 00:08:03.453
against the Russian economy.

00:08:04.550 --> 00:08:06.710
Sanctions are really only as
strong as the weakest link.

00:08:06.710 --> 00:08:08.670
If you have differences in designations,

00:08:08.670 --> 00:08:10.730
differences in who's being targeted,

00:08:10.730 --> 00:08:14.000
you can clearly take advantage of that.

00:08:14.000 --> 00:08:17.100
Historically, the Europeans,
including U.K. pre-Brexit,

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:19.150
have not been particularly aggressive

00:08:19.150 --> 00:08:20.310
on the enforcement fund.

00:08:20.310 --> 00:08:23.430
In the EU side, sanctions
implementation is done

00:08:23.430 --> 00:08:24.780
by Brussels but enforcement is done

00:08:24.780 --> 00:08:27.530
by the 27 states, member
states independently.

00:08:27.530 --> 00:08:30.080
And of course, each state
has different capacities,

00:08:30.080 --> 00:08:31.140
different political interests

00:08:31.140 --> 00:08:32.730
and different concerns.

00:08:32.730 --> 00:08:34.320
And therefore, enforcement has been

00:08:34.320 --> 00:08:37.250
somewhat lacking compared
to the United States.

00:08:37.250 --> 00:08:38.270
And so I am concerned

00:08:38.270 --> 00:08:40.040
about whether we're gonna get enforcement,

00:08:40.040 --> 00:08:41.700
which is actually where the teeth can

00:08:41.700 --> 00:08:43.650
actually come in to sanctions.

00:08:45.740 --> 00:08:46.760
I mean look at the history

00:08:46.760 --> 00:08:49.318
of sanctions in the two
most high profile cases,

00:08:49.318 --> 00:08:50.484
Iran and North Korea.

00:08:50.484 --> 00:08:52.540
It hasn't worked, at all.

00:08:52.540 --> 00:08:55.010
If anything, it's only
strengthened the regime.

00:08:55.010 --> 00:08:57.110
So there is a real
question about sanctions

00:08:57.110 --> 00:09:00.100
as a tool, in a situation like this.

00:09:00.100 --> 00:09:00.940
Will it really work,

00:09:00.940 --> 00:09:03.673
or will they perversely strengthen Putin?

00:09:05.700 --> 00:09:06.920
So if Vladimir Putin doesn't care

00:09:06.920 --> 00:09:09.060
about sanctions against his officials,

00:09:09.060 --> 00:09:10.180
he doesn't care about sanctions

00:09:10.180 --> 00:09:12.100
against Russian state companies,

00:09:12.100 --> 00:09:13.670
he absolutely profoundly cares

00:09:13.670 --> 00:09:15.440
about sanctions against Russian oligarchs

00:09:15.440 --> 00:09:17.740
because those oligarchs hold his money.

00:09:17.740 --> 00:09:19.352
And you can just look at his reaction,

00:09:19.352 --> 00:09:22.340
when the British
government started talking

00:09:22.340 --> 00:09:24.070
about sanctioning oligarchs,
that was the first

00:09:24.070 --> 00:09:26.440
moment when he started
threatening nuclear war.

00:09:26.440 --> 00:09:28.150
It's the thing he cares most about.

00:09:28.150 --> 00:09:29.765
Vladimir Putin is a man who values money

00:09:29.765 --> 00:09:31.643
more than human life.

00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:35.240
But not everyone agrees

00:09:35.240 --> 00:09:37.970
that president Putin can be targeted

00:09:37.970 --> 00:09:40.160
by going after his foreign assets.

00:09:40.160 --> 00:09:44.500
There are many who think
that there are oligarchs

00:09:44.500 --> 00:09:47.690
in the West that are
essentially Putin's banker

00:09:47.690 --> 00:09:50.640
but in reality I've had
other people tell me,

00:09:50.640 --> 00:09:51.520
he doesn't need that,

00:09:51.520 --> 00:09:53.260
he has the entire Russian state

00:09:53.260 --> 00:09:55.360
at his disposal to use.

00:09:55.360 --> 00:09:58.150
He doesn't need someone
else to be his banker,

00:09:58.150 --> 00:10:00.920
because he has all these
state-run companies

00:10:00.920 --> 00:10:03.010
that he can use the cashflow from

00:10:03.010 --> 00:10:04.353
to do whatever he wants.

00:10:05.660 --> 00:10:07.050
And while targeted sanctions

00:10:07.050 --> 00:10:09.410
may not change Putin's mind,

00:10:09.410 --> 00:10:11.950
sanctions on the Russian
economy are being felt

00:10:11.950 --> 00:10:13.333
by ordinary people.

00:10:13.333 --> 00:10:14.170
The sanctions will

00:10:14.170 --> 00:10:17.230
essentially decimate the
Russian middle class,

00:10:17.230 --> 00:10:19.300
which many believe is key

00:10:19.300 --> 00:10:22.410
to building some kind of democratic state

00:10:22.410 --> 00:10:23.660
and I think there's an assumption

00:10:23.660 --> 00:10:28.224
that you inflict so much
pain on ordinary Russians,

00:10:28.224 --> 00:10:30.000
that they will rise up

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:33.500
and demand changes or
overthrow the government.

00:10:33.500 --> 00:10:37.460
And again, I think that
underestimates Russian history

00:10:37.460 --> 00:10:40.793
and the power of the Kremlin.

00:10:43.400 --> 00:10:44.233
For Browder,

00:10:44.233 --> 00:10:47.370
sanctions don't need to
have any higher ambitions

00:10:47.370 --> 00:10:50.400
than throwing a spanner
in Putin's war machine.

00:10:50.400 --> 00:10:52.277
It's a hugely expensive war, a billion,

00:10:52.277 --> 00:10:55.040
$2 billion a day is spent on this war.

00:10:55.040 --> 00:10:57.570
He doesn't have access to
his central bank reserves.

00:10:57.570 --> 00:10:59.920
He doesn't have access
to his oligarch capital.

00:11:00.920 --> 00:11:03.890
He doesn't have access
to external financing.

00:11:03.890 --> 00:11:05.660
And the purpose of this is not

00:11:05.660 --> 00:11:08.150
to get somebody to change
his mind, it's to make sure

00:11:08.150 --> 00:11:10.300
that he just doesn't have
enough money to do it

00:11:10.300 --> 00:11:11.860
and this is how we won the Cold War.

00:11:11.860 --> 00:11:13.630
We basically bled them dry

00:11:13.630 --> 00:11:15.080
and we have to do that again.

00:11:19.970 --> 00:11:22.170
How this all plays out
isn't entirely clear

00:11:22.170 --> 00:11:24.620
because we've never been here before.

00:11:24.620 --> 00:11:27.410
Russia's now the most
sanctioned country in the world

00:11:27.410 --> 00:11:28.600
and it's at war.

00:11:28.600 --> 00:11:30.113
We have not been here before.

00:11:31.430 --> 00:11:35.390
So, it'll be an interesting test case.

00:11:35.390 --> 00:11:39.680
Can you cripple an economy

00:11:39.680 --> 00:11:43.020
and starve it of the resources
it needs to wage war?

00:11:43.020 --> 00:11:46.400
Well, that depends on a number of factors.

00:11:46.400 --> 00:11:47.410
If China comes in

00:11:47.410 --> 00:11:50.561
and bails out Russia with weapons

00:11:50.561 --> 00:11:54.230
and other financial support,
then they could continue

00:11:54.230 --> 00:11:57.913
to wage this war for quite a while.

00:11:58.970 --> 00:11:59.803
So I think the way

00:11:59.803 --> 00:12:01.312
that China could potentially aid Russia is

00:12:01.312 --> 00:12:03.730
by serving as a payment conduit, right?

00:12:03.730 --> 00:12:04.870
So Russian institutions,

00:12:04.870 --> 00:12:06.740
certainly the big ones have
essentially been shut off

00:12:06.740 --> 00:12:08.170
from the international community

00:12:08.170 --> 00:12:10.120
but Chinese institutions
of course haven't been

00:12:10.120 --> 00:12:11.670
and there's no reason
that you can't sort of,

00:12:11.670 --> 00:12:14.573
funnel a payment from rubels to renminbi,

00:12:14.573 --> 00:12:16.900
and then out, if you go via Shanghai,

00:12:16.900 --> 00:12:19.400
or Beijing, or buy Hong
Kong dollars in Hong Kong.

00:12:20.810 --> 00:12:22.790
I'm not sure China wants to sort of,

00:12:22.790 --> 00:12:25.560
risk their rise, their sort of soft power

00:12:25.560 --> 00:12:28.700
on sort of, getting into
bed very very closely

00:12:28.700 --> 00:12:30.820
and intimately with
someone who is so reviled

00:12:30.820 --> 00:12:32.320
on a international basis.

00:12:32.320 --> 00:12:34.980
If the U.S. then responds
with secondary sanctions

00:12:34.980 --> 00:12:38.450
on China for dealing with Russia,

00:12:38.450 --> 00:12:41.830
then that cuts out that other escape route

00:12:41.830 --> 00:12:43.640
that Putin potentially has.

00:12:43.640 --> 00:12:47.313
So, the world is unified,
but not entirely unified.

